  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule itself.",
    "The query's very high lipophilicity (logD 5.89) and unfavorable solubility prior could lower absorption, but no affirmative low-F evidence or dose/formulation data are available.",
    "Metabolic first-pass and efflux behavior for the query are not directly measured; transfer from structurally related contexts is qualitative.",
    "Dose and formulation for the query are unknown, which can affect absolute bioavailability."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "All visible L1 records are direct human absolute oral bioavailability measurements with values ≥43%, and none support F<20%. The most structurally relevant contexts (glasdegib, AG-221, ondansetron) show 50-77% absolute oral bioavailability in fasted/fed humans despite lipophilic, poorly soluble features. The query's poor solubility prior is a limitation but not affirmative evidence of low F, so F≥20% is better supported."
}

